menu "ble-ota Configuration"

    config BLE_OTA_PAIRING_PASSKEY
        int "BLE pairing passkey (6 digits)"
        default 123456
        range 0 999999
        depends on BT_NIMBLE_STATIC_PASSKEY
        help
            Fixed passkey used for Passkey Entry pairing (see main.c's Security Manager setup
            and led_service.c's Config characteristic). Whoever pairs with this device will need
            to type this exact 6-digit number into their phone's system pairing prompt.

            Educational note: this value is checked into source control and shipped in the
            companion Android app's bundled firmware, so it does not function as a real secret -
            it demonstrates the mechanics of Passkey Entry pairing (as opposed to Just Works),
            not real protection against a man-in-the-middle. A deployment that actually needs
            that protection would need a passkey unique per device, distributed out-of-band.

endmenu
